{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791224133,"nonce":"DAgBTcsrSREytiRUE9M5tHljZYI=","message":"Cause: the hang is inside xwindow's wait. A sample of the hung process (30 min, 0.2% CPU) shows the main thread in __hl_window_wait_variant -\u003e -[NSApplication run] -\u003e nextEventMatchingMask -\u003e mach_msg, so window.wait(timeout) never returned although WindowedApp's loop never asks for more than 0.1s (FRAME_WAIT_LIMIT or 1/120 or 0.1, capped by timers and ASHUI_WINDOW_SECONDS). With no events arriving (the window behind others, nothing animating) the wait blocks for good. Leftover demo windows from earlier runs were not the cause: it still hung in 2 of 3 runs with no other ash process. Handed to the xwindow-fa session.","files":null}]}